      "description": "With 6 mana available (2 Mountains + 2 City of Traitors) and the opponent at 11 life, casting Simian Spirit Guide as a vanilla 2/2 for 3 mana is far inferior to casting Pyrogoyf for 4 mana. The graveyard contains multiple card types (artifact from Chalice, enchantment from Blood Moon, creature from Magus, land from City of Traitors, sorcery from opponent's Ponder, instant from Lotus Petal) making Pyrogoyf approximately a 5/6 or larger that also deals its power as damage to any target on ETB - potentially dealing 5+ damage directly to the opponent who is at 11 life.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Simian Spirit Guide as a 2/2 creature for {2}{R}",
      "better_line": "Cast Pyrogoyf for {3}{R} using City of Traitors + Mountain, dealing approximately 5 damage to the opponent on ETB (bringing them to ~6 life) while deploying a large threat. Could potentially even cast two threats this turn with the remaining mana.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 108,
      "player": "Gem25F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 134,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With Blood Moon already on the battlefield, casting Simian Spirit Guide as a 2/2 creature for 3 mana is low-impact. With 5 mana available (Mountain + 2x City of Traitors), Gem25F Johnny could hardcast Fury as a 3/3 double striker, representing 6 damage per attack against an opponent at 11 life with no blockers. Even though Fury's ETB has no creature/planeswalker targets, the body is far superior for closing out the game against a Sneak Attack player who could combo off at any moment.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Simian Spirit Guide as a 2/2 creature for {2}{R}",
      "better_line": "Hardcast Fury for {3}{R}{R} using Mountain + 2x City of Traitors to deploy a 3/3 double striker, threatening lethal in 2 attacks against the opponent at 11 life",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 108,
      "player": "Gem25F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 134,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Blood Moon is already on the battlefield, making Magus of the Moon entirely redundant. Meanwhile, the opponent is at 11 life with Sneak Attack threatening to end the game. Deploying actual threats like Pyrogoyf (which would deal ~5 ETB damage based on card types in graveyards) would put real pressure on the opponent.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Magus of the Moon, which duplicates the Blood Moon already in play",
      "better_line": "Cast Pyrogoyf (3R) using City of Traitors + Mountain mana. With ~5 card types in graveyards, it would deal 5 damage on ETB (putting opponent to 6) and present a significant clock, while also being a body to block if opponent uses Sneak Attack.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 108,
      "player": "Gem25F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 134,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "With 5 red mana available (3 Mountains + 2 City of Traitors turned to Mountains by Blood Moon), casting Simian Spirit Guide as a vanilla 2/2 instead of Pyrogoyf which would be a 5/6 (5 card types in graveyards) AND deal 5 damage to the opponent on ETB (dropping them from 11 to 6 life) is a massive missed opportunity. The opponent has Sneak Attack active and could end the game at any moment, so maximizing damage output is critical.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Simian Spirit Guide as a 2/2 creature for {2}{R}",
      "better_line": "Cast Pyrogoyf for {3}{R}, targeting the opponent with its ETB for 5 damage (5 card types in graveyards), creating a 5/6 body and dropping opponent to 6 life. This applies massive pressure against a Sneak Attack deck that needs to be raced.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 109,
      "player": "Gem25F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 153,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With Blood Moon/Magus making all lands Mountains (3 R available), exiling Simian Spirit Guide would provide a 4th mana to cast The One Ring, which is a significantly more impactful play than Broadside Bombardiers. The One Ring provides protection from everything for the turn (critical with opponent's Sneak Attack threatening huge creatures), indestructibility, and card advantage engine. Broadside Bombardiers is a 2/2 that's relatively low-impact.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to cast Broadside Bombardiers for 3 mana",
      "better_line": "Exile Simian Spirit Guide for {R}, then cast The One Ring for {4}. The protection from everything shields against Sneak Attack threats, and the card draw engine helps find more threats to close the game.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 116,
      "player": "Gem25F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 164,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The opponent has Sneak Attack on the battlefield, which is an extremely dangerous threat. The One Ring was castable (3 lands + exile Simian Spirit Guide = 4 mana) and would have provided protection from everything until next turn, shutting down any Sneak Attack activations, while also providing a card draw engine. Instead, a 2/2 haste creature was deployed that applies minimal pressure.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Broadside Bombardiers, a 2/2 menace haste creature",
      "better_line": "Exile Simian Spirit Guide for {R}, tap 3 Mountains to cast The One Ring. This provides protection from everything until next turn (critical defense against Sneak Attack) and sets up a powerful card draw engine for subsequent turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 118,
      "player": "Gem25F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 170,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Under Blood Moon, all three land options (Wasteland, Cavern of Souls, Eye of Ugin) would enter as Mountains tapping for {R}. There's no downside to playing one, and the extra mana source provides flexibility, especially with Sneak Attack on board needing {R} activations to put Atraxa into play.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to play a land this turn.",
      "better_line": "Play Wasteland (or any of the three lands) as it becomes a Mountain under Blood Moon, providing an additional red mana source at no cost. This is especially important with Sneak Attack in play and two Ataxas in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 118,
      "player": "Qwen3 Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 171,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to play a land when holding three lands (Wasteland, Cavern of Souls, Eye of Ugin). Under Blood Moon, all would enter as Mountains providing {R}. There's no downside to playing any of them, and the extra mana source could be relevant for multiple Sneak Attack activations or casting spells.",
      "action_taken": "Chose not to play any land, missing the land drop entirely.",
      "better_line": "Play Wasteland (or Cavern of Souls) as it becomes a Mountain under Blood Moon, providing an additional {R} source at no cost. Wasteland is the least valuable card to 'use up' as a Mountain since its special ability is nullified by Blood Moon anyway.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 119,
      "player": "Qwen3 Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 173,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 9 life with Blood Moon already in play making Magus of the Moon redundant. Broadside Bombardiers' Boast ability could sacrifice Magus of the Moon to deal 5 damage (2 + CMC 3), putting opponent to 4 life. This is essentially free damage since Blood Moon already maintains the nonbasic-lands-are-Mountains lock.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to use Broadside Bombardiers' Boast ability, passing without dealing any additional damage.",
      "better_line": "Activate Broadside Bombardiers' Boast ability, sacrificing Magus of the Moon to deal 5 damage to the opponent, putting them from 9 to 4 life. Blood Moon remains in play to maintain the lock.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 123,
      "player": "Gem25F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 179,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Veil of Summer (MV 1) is permanently dead while Chalice of the Void on 1 is in play - it will always be countered. Stock Up could become castable if Blood Moon is removed (e.g., by channeling Boseiju to destroy it), after which Volcanic Islands would produce blue mana again.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Stock Up",
      "better_line": "Discard Veil of Summer, which is a completely dead card due to Chalice on 1, while Stock Up has a realistic path to being castable if Blood Moon is removed via Boseiju's channel ability.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 127,
      "player": "Qwen3 Vorthos",
      "decision_index": 190,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Player has lethal on board: attack with Magus of the Moon (2) + Broadside Bombardiers (2) for 4 damage (opponent to 5), then use Bombardiers' Boast to sacrifice Magus of the Moon (CMC 3) dealing 2+3=5 damage for exact lethal. The player's reasoning shows no awareness of this lethal line, focusing instead on incremental value plays. Playing Urza's Saga first is fine, but only if they follow up with the lethal attack.",
      "action_taken": "Appears to be playing Urza's Saga as land drop, with no mention of recognizing lethal on board",
      "better_line": "Play Urza's Saga if desired, then immediately go to combat, attack with both Magus of the Moon and Broadside Bombardiers, then activate Bombardiers' Boast sacrificing Magus for exactly 5 damage to opponent at 5 life = lethal",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 127,
      "player": "Gem25F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 187,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Missed lethal. Pyrogoyf's ETB deals damage equal to its power (6, based on ~6 card types in graveyards) to any target, which could target the opponent at 9 life. Combined with attacking with Magus of the Moon (2) and Broadside Bombardiers (2), that's 10 damage total against 9 life. Instead, chose to play Urza's Saga which becomes a basic Mountain under Blood Moon and does nothing.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to play Urza's Saga (which is blanked by their own Blood Moon into just a Mountain)",
      "better_line": "Cast Pyrogoyf (using City of Traitors + Mountain for mana), target opponent with ETB for 6 damage, then attack with Magus of the Moon and Broadside Bombardiers for 4 more damage = 10 total, lethal against 9 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 128,
