      "decision_index": 196,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Broadside Bombardiers attacked this turn, enabling its Boast ability. Sacrificing Magus of the Moon (CMC 3) to the Boast would deal 2+3=5 damage directly to the opponent at 7 life, bringing them to 2. Instead, the player appears to be casting Simian Spirit Guide as a vanilla 2/2, completely ignoring a powerful activated ability that nearly delivers lethal damage.",
      "action_taken": "Appears to have cast Simian Spirit Guide as a 2/2 creature instead of using Broadside Bombardiers' Boast ability.",
      "better_line": "Activate Broadside Bombardiers' Boast ability, sacrificing Magus of the Moon (CMC 3) to deal 5 damage to opponent's face (7→2 life). This nearly guarantees lethal next turn with any attacker. Could also sacrifice a Chalice of the Void (CMC 0) for 2 damage if wanting to preserve Magus, though Magus is less important with Blood Moon already in play.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 134,
      "player": "Gem25F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 203,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Missed lethal. Broadside Bombardiers attacked this turn, enabling its Boast ability. Evoking Fury (exile a red card like Pyrogoyf) then using Bombardiers' Boast to sacrifice Fury deals 2 + 5 (Fury's mana value) = 7 damage to opponent at exactly 7 life, which is lethal.",
